The campaign already targeted macOS through disk images; what Microsoft reported on 2026-05-06 is its shift to ClickFix Terminal commands, along three execution paths of which only one is a one-line shell pipeline. The stealers replace installed Ledger Wallet, Trezor Suite and Exodus apps with trojanized versions fetched from their C2, not DMG copies, and detection follows Microsoft's guidance on Terminal sessions, utility sequences and data staging.
